  64:     """
  65:     Render the lower grey slot array by replacing each colored control pixel with the matching legend template.
  66: 
  67:     Input structure
  68:     A background grid has a top legend: each colored marker sits one row above and one column left of a
  69:     2x2 template drawn in a shared template ink color.  Below it is a rectangular array of 2x2 grey slots,
  70:     where a slot may contain one colored control pixel in place of grey.
  71: 
  72:     Rule
  73:     Read the legend as color -> 2x2 template mask.  Convert the lower slot array into a compact array with
  74:     the same row/column layout and one background separator row/column between neighboring tiles.  Empty
  75:     grey slots become blank tiles; a colored slot becomes that color's legend mask recolored with the
  76:     control color.
  77: 
  78:     Key insight
  79:     The colored pixel in a grey slot names which top legend template to stamp; its position inside the slot
  80:     is irrelevant.
